# peeryard patch ergo/002: MempoolAuditor: rebroadcast a pooled transaction together with its in-pool ancestors
# upstream: ergoplatform/ergo#2573 (proposed); origin, witness and responses in patches.json
commit 817f99276338c70424fe6f1c9252addbd9ed5b9b
Author: cafebedouin <cafebedouin@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 22:04:02 2026 -0500

    MempoolAuditor: announce a rebroadcast transaction only after its in-pool parents
    
    The ancestor walk puts the in-pool parents of each selected transaction ahead of it, but the input check
    counted the outputs of every transaction in the round, including a parent it had just skipped. In a pooled
    chain whose root has inputs in neither the state nor the pool, the root was skipped and its descendants were
    announced without it, and a peer declines those as before. Walk the round parents first and accept a
    transaction only if each input is in the state or is created by a transaction already accepted in this round,
    so a transaction is never announced without its in-pool parents, also when the depth bound cuts the walk short.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

